<section aria-labelledby="rady-h" class="rady" id="rady">
<div class="obal">
<div class="hlava">
<h2 data-odhalit="" id="rady-h">Tips from the workshop</h2>
<p data-odhalit="">This is what drivers {{ city_in }} ask us most often. If you’re not sure, give us a call or book straight away.</p>
</div>
<div class="clanky">
<details class="clanek">
<summary><h3>The engine warning light is on. Can I keep driving?</h3><p>It depends on whether it’s steady or flashing. That tells you how quickly to act.</p><span aria-hidden="true" class="plus"></span></summary>
<div class="telo"><div>
<p>When the engine light <strong>stays on</strong>, the control unit has logged a fault in engine management or the emissions system. You can usually drive on carefully, but don’t wait weeks for a diagnosis. A small fault, such as a bad sensor, can raise fuel consumption or damage other parts.</p>
<p>When the light <strong>flashes</strong>, the engine is usually misfiring. Unburnt fuel gets into the exhaust and can destroy the catalytic converter. Slow down, avoid long trips and have the car checked as soon as possible. If the engine loses power and goes into limp mode, better not drive on.</p>
<p>During diagnostics we read the fault codes. A code shows where to look, not what exactly to replace, so we confirm the cause by measuring and only then quote the repair. <a href="#objednat">Book diagnostics</a></p>
</div></div>
</details>
<details class="clanek">
<summary><h3>When to replace brake pads and brake fluid</h3><p>Squealing, vibration and longer stopping distances are signs not worth putting off.</p><span aria-hidden="true" class="plus"></span></summary>
<div class="telo"><div>
<p>Depending on how you drive, pads last tens of thousands of miles – less in town than on the motorway. A metallic squeal when braking is usually the wear indicator telling you the lining is running out. Vibration in the steering wheel or pedal often means warped discs.</p>
<p>Brake fluid absorbs moisture from the air. With water its boiling point drops, and on a long downhill the brakes can go “soft”. That’s why manufacturers usually prescribe a change every two years, regardless of mileage.</p>
<p>During a check we measure pad and disc thickness and test the fluid. We only replace what is worn. <a href="#objednat">Book a brake check</a></p>
</div></div>
</details>
<details class="clanek">
<summary><h3>How to prepare for your vehicle inspection and pass first time</h3><p>The most common faults can be found and fixed before you go.</p><span aria-hidden="true" class="plus"></span></summary>
<div class="telo"><div>
<p>How often your car needs an inspection depends on where you live and how old the car is. You’ll find the due date on your last inspection report. Take your vehicle registration document with you.</p>
<p>Cars most often fail on lights (bulbs out or headlights badly aimed), brakes (uneven performance), play in the steering and suspension, fluid leaks and emissions. Check your tyres too: tread depth must be at least 1.6 mm.</p>
<p>When preparing for the inspection we check what the inspector looks at and fix anything that wouldn’t pass. <a href="#objednat">Book inspection prep</a></p>
</div></div>
</details>
<details class="clanek">
<summary><h3>Timing belt: why not to wait until it snaps</h3><p>Replacing it on schedule costs a fraction of an engine repair after it breaks.</p><span aria-hidden="true" class="plus"></span></summary>
<div class="telo"><div>
<p>The timing belt keeps the pistons and valves in sync. In most modern engines, if it snaps the valves hit the pistons, and repairing the cylinder head costs many times more than replacing the belt.</p>
<p>The manufacturer sets the interval in both miles and years – whichever comes first. A belt ages even on cars that do few miles. We replace the whole kit: belt, tensioner and idler pulleys, and usually the water pump when the belt drives it.</p>
<p>Engines with a timing chain often have no fixed interval, but the chain stretches over time. A warning sign is rattling just after a cold start. <a href="#objednat">Book a timing belt change</a></p>
</div></div>
</details>
</div>
</div>
</section>

